### Fixture disposable HTTPS only — examples, not a runnable bulk suite.
### Supply {{fixtureBaseUrl}} (random loopback port, never 8443), fixture-only tokens
### and random passwords from an isolated process. Trust that fixture's certificate.
### Do not persist variables, responses, history or secrets in a Postman/IDE profile.
### Use scripts/manual-http.cjs as documented in README.acceptance.md for actual observations.
### Do not send X-Forwarded-For or use real accounts; select each request individually.

### Login ADMIN — 200 Bearer, ADMIN (bootstrap forced change must already be completed)
POST {{fixtureBaseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "username": "{{fixtureAdminUsername}}",
  "password": "{{fixtureAdminPassword}}"
}

### Login USER — 200 Bearer, USER
POST {{fixtureBaseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "username": "{{fixtureUserUsername}}",
  "password": "{{fixtureUserPassword}}"
}

### Wrong password — 401 UNAUTHORIZED; never distinguish unknown user
POST {{fixtureBaseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "username": "{{fixtureUserUsername}}",
  "password": "{{fixtureWrongPassword}}"
}

### Unknown fixture user — 401 UNAUTHORIZED
POST {{fixtureBaseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "username": "{{fixtureNonexistentUsername}}",
  "password": "{{fixtureWrongPassword}}"
}

### Correct password of explicitly locked disposable target — 403 ACCOUNT_DISABLED
POST {{fixtureBaseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "username": "{{fixtureLockedUsername}}",
  "password": "{{fixtureLockedPassword}}"
}

### Rate limit: repeat only on a separate disposable user up to configured threshold;
### observe 429 TOO_MANY_ATTEMPTS and Retry-After, then stop. No automatic loop.
POST {{fixtureBaseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "username": "{{fixtureRateLimitUsername}}",
  "password": "{{fixtureWrongPassword}}"
}

### Invalid body — 400 VALIDATION_ERROR
POST {{fixtureBaseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "username": "a",
  "password": ""
}

### No bearer — 401 UNAUTHORIZED
GET {{fixtureBaseUrl}}/api/auth/me
Accept: application/json

### Correct bearer — 200, no password hash
GET {{fixtureBaseUrl}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{fixtureUserToken}}
Accept: application/json

### Public config — 200 without token
GET {{fixtureBaseUrl}}/api/public/config
Accept: application/json

### Register — 201 USER regardless of supplied role; valid fresh disposable username/email
POST {{fixtureBaseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "username": "{{fixtureNewUsername}}",
  "password": "{{fixtureNewPassword}}",
  "fullName": "Disposable example",
  "email": "{{fixtureNewEmail}}",
  "role": "ADMIN"
}

### Register duplicate — 409 USERNAME_TAKEN (same username, distinct email)
POST {{fixtureBaseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "username": "{{fixtureNewUsername}}",
  "password": "{{fixtureNewPassword}}",
  "fullName": "Disposable duplicate",
  "email": "{{fixtureOtherNewEmail}}"
}

### Change password — 200, new JWT, mustChangePassword=false
POST {{fixtureBaseUrl}}/api/auth/change-password
Authorization: Bearer {{fixtureUserToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "currentPassword": "{{fixtureUserPassword}}",
  "newPassword": "{{fixtureNewUserPassword}}"
}

### Wrong current password — 400 VALIDATION_ERROR
POST {{fixtureBaseUrl}}/api/auth/change-password
Authorization: Bearer {{fixtureUserToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "currentPassword": "{{fixtureWrongPassword}}",
  "newPassword": "{{fixtureNewUserPassword}}"
}

### Owner's Gmail list — 200, no credentials
GET {{fixtureBaseUrl}}/api/gmail-accounts
Authorization: Bearer {{fixtureUserToken}}
Accept: application/json

### OAuth authorize — 200 URL + poll token, CREATE default
### Do not follow real Google URL in local fixture. Use manual-http.cjs callback mode.
GET {{fixtureBaseUrl}}/api/oauth2/authorize-url
Authorization: Bearer {{fixtureUserToken}}
Accept: application/json

### Poll one local fixture session — 202 PENDING / 200 terminal / 410 consumed
### Never persist or display poll token.
GET {{fixtureBaseUrl}}/api/oauth2/link/poll?pollToken={{fixturePollToken}}
Authorization: Bearer {{fixtureUserToken}}
Accept: application/json

### Invalid synthetic callback — 200 HTML failure, not JSON
GET {{fixtureBaseUrl}}/api/oauth2/callback?code=mock_code&state=invalid_or_expired_state
Accept: text/html

### Incompatible media — expected 406 NOT_ACCEPTABLE in fixed source
GET {{fixtureBaseUrl}}/api/oauth2/callback?code=mock_code&state=invalid_or_expired_state
Accept: application/json

### Change settings only on isolated fixture; snapshot original values first.
### Disable OAuth and keep App Password enabled — 200
PUT {{fixtureBaseUrl}}/api/admin/settings
Authorization: Bearer {{fixtureAdminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "settings": {
    "ALLOW_OAUTH2_LINK": "false",
    "ALLOW_APP_PASSWORD_LINK": "true"
  }
}

### Now verify public config, then OAuth authorize — 403 FEATURE_DISABLED
GET {{fixtureBaseUrl}}/api/public/config
Accept: application/json

###
GET {{fixtureBaseUrl}}/api/oauth2/authorize-url
Authorization: Bearer {{fixtureUserToken}}
Accept: application/json

### Restore saved fixture values (do not assume defaults on existing service)
PUT {{fixtureBaseUrl}}/api/admin/settings
Authorization: Bearer {{fixtureAdminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "settings": {
    "ALLOW_OAUTH2_LINK": "{{fixtureOriginalOAuthFlag}}",
    "ALLOW_APP_PASSWORD_LINK": "{{fixtureOriginalAppPasswordFlag}}"
  }
}

### Register-disabled case: set ALLOW_REGISTRATION=false using admin settings,
### confirm public config, then send VALID fresh body (not missing body). Expect 403.
POST {{fixtureBaseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "username": "{{fixtureDisabledRegisterUsername}}",
  "password": "{{fixtureNewPassword}}",
  "fullName": "Disposable disabled register probe",
  "email": "{{fixtureDisabledRegisterEmail}}"
}

### Missing link ID — 404 NOT_FOUND; never guess an existing user's mailbox ID
DELETE {{fixtureBaseUrl}}/api/gmail-accounts/{{fixtureNonexistentGmailId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{fixtureUserToken}}
Accept: application/json

### Restore the exact original fixture setting values and stop the harness after observations.
